From: mscharged-port
Subject: Keep GameSpy on its Revolution platform code in Windows builds
Upstream-base: 9046e67aa2077a7eb4ed6e28c9df3c1d3b368f84
Classification: native platform selection; no change on the Wii or POSIX hosts.

GameSpy picks its platform code with the compiler's platform macros, and
in several places tests _WIN32 before _REVOLUTION. The online sources
are compiled with _REVOLUTION, as on the Wii, but a Windows compiler also
predefines _WIN32, so these places took the Win32 branch:
gsPlatformThread.c included win32/gsThreadWin32.c, which the decomp does
not have, and the others would use OutputDebugString, MessageBox,
QueryPerformanceCounter, _fstat and #pragma comment(lib) instead of the
Revolution code the rest of GameSpy expects.

Each of these _WIN32 tests now also requires that _REVOLUTION is not
defined. _WIN32 is never defined on the Wii or on POSIX hosts, where
nothing changes. sb_server.c's _WIN32 test is left alone: it also needs
GM_2B, which no build defines.

diff --git a/src/RVL_SDK/gamespy/GP/gpiTransfer.c b/src/RVL_SDK/gamespy/GP/gpiTransfer.c
index 9a4b0fe..c44e748 100644
--- a/src/RVL_SDK/gamespy/GP/gpiTransfer.c
+++ b/src/RVL_SDK/gamespy/GP/gpiTransfer.c
@@ -14,7 +14,7 @@ Please see the GameSpy Presence SDK documentation for more information
 // INCLUDES
 //////////
 #include <stdlib.h>
-#ifdef _WIN32
+#if defined(_WIN32) && !defined(_REVOLUTION)
 #include <sys/stat.h>
 #endif
 #include <string.h>
@@ -1376,7 +1376,7 @@ GPIBool gpiGetTransferFileInfo(
     int* size,
     gsi_time* modTime)
 {
-#ifdef _WIN32
+#if defined(_WIN32) && !defined(_REVOLUTION)
     struct _stat stats;
 
     if (_fstat(_fileno(file), &stats) != 0)
